# Agelessones First Mod: version history

Newest first. Keep `ModVersion` in `FirstModPlugin.cs` in sync with the top entry.

```text
  1.51.51 RED HAMMER: the loose parts (wood frames, rock formations) of a structure were all removed in one frame at the very end, which could lag. They are now removed a few per step like the building pieces (DemolishPiecesPerStep / DemolishStepSeconds).
  1.51.50 RED HAMMER: everything it removes now drops its resources. Pieces already did and loose breakable parts already dropped their loot; rock formations (which Ashlands and other world structures use) were removed silently in the whole-structure removal, they are now broken part by part so what they hold drops too.
  1.51.49 RED HAMMER REWORK: it removes ANYTHING the world made (ruins, fortresses, Deep North structures, loose breakable parts), and never touches anything a player built or placed (message: "Built by a player: the Red hammer leaves it alone."). Middle click removes only the piece you look at (its materials drop); Shift + middle click removes the whole structure, and a player's building next to it is never swept up with it. It needs no workbench and no build menu: its middle click is also read by the mod itself, so it works whatever the game's own build rules say (a short pause after each click stops a double removal). Wards are still respected (setting DemolishRespectWards; turn it off if it should ignore them too).
  1.51.48 CLEANUP (from your latest log): 44 warnings written by the mod itself are gone. The game translation lookup (Localization) was searched again on every call and wrote "Could not find field ... instance" 42 times a session; it is now looked up once. The Red hammer registration and the inventory cell probe no longer write their "could not find method / field" warnings either (they fall back by themselves, nothing was wrong). No change in behaviour.
  1.51.47 FIX (from your friend log, 5914 lines of "Im still nto the owner" and "but they are already the owner"): the LOOT VACUUM of two players asked for ownership of the same dropped items over and over (every 0.2 s per item). It now asks at most once every 3-5 s per item, at a random moment so two players do not ask in step. The log hiding of 1.51.45 also covers the two new line kinds. (Not related to the door problem: nothing in the log mentions a door.)
  1.51.46 FIX (the "Im still the owner" spam, found from your log: nobody had a chest open): the auto feed of two players taking smelters and chests from each other. (1) A smelter owned by another player is no longer taken over (v1.51.28 did that); it is fed by asking its owner (the request goes to the owner), only when it clearly has room, at most every 4 s per smelter. (2) A chest that another player took from you a moment after you took it is left alone for 20 s instead of being taken back at once. (3) The shield generator feed no longer takes ownership either (its owner feeds it). The log hiding of 1.51.45 stays as a safety net.
  1.51.45 FIX (log spam): the game line "Im still the owner" was written many times a second. Lines like it are now dropped before they are written (1. General / HideOwnerLogSpam, on), so the log stays readable and the time spent writing them is saved. This hides the symptom only: if you can, send a few lines from around the first one (the lines just before it) so the cause, probably a chest or station changing owner back and forth between two players, can be found.
  1.51.44 NEW (37. Lightning Strike Staff / StrikesWhereYouPoint): first try at making the Lightning Strike staff strike where you point. Written without the game files, so it sets every spread-like value (accuracy, scatter, spread, random offset) of the staff attack and of what it fires to 0, and writes all the values the game has for the staff to LogOutput.log once at start, as [StrikeAim] lines. If the strikes are still scattered, send me those lines: they show where the scatter really comes from and I fix it exactly. StaffPrefabNames can name the item if it is not found by itself.
  1.51.43 FIX: the skill carry weight bonus now also works on the starting carry weight you set yourself (4. Player Cheats / CustomCarryWeight): the multiplier is applied to that number, and the bonus is added after the custom value is set. With no custom weight it still works on the game 300.
  1.51.42 NEW (36. Skill Carry Weight): your carry weight grows with the Run skill (setting Skill: Run, Jump, Swim or Sneak): your normal 300 is multiplied by up to MultiplierAtSkill100 (default 2 = 600 at skill 100, growing evenly from 1 at skill 0). Added on top of the game result, so the Megingjord belt and other limit changes are untouched. EnableSkillCarry false turns it off.
  1.51.41 NEW (35. Skill Speed): running and swimming get faster as the Run and Swim skills rise, growing smoothly from nothing at skill 0 to RunSpeedBonusAtMax (default +15%) and SwimSpeedBonusAtMax (default +50%, swimming is very slow) at skill 100. It comes on top of the game own skill bonus. Set a value to 0 or EnableSkillSpeed to false to turn it off; the normal speeds are put back.
  1.51.40 PERFORMANCE: the smelter auto feed took about 6 ms every pass (your log). Each smelter looked up every chest on its own (ward check included) and used slow reflection for every call. The chests near you are now looked up once per pass and shared by all smelters, and the smelter and chest fields and methods are looked up once. Same behaviour, a fraction of the time.
  1.51.39 NEW (34. Trollstav / TrollsNeverAttackPlayers, on): the trolls summoned by the Trollstav (the troll staff) no longer attack players. The game makes them attack everything nearby, you included; now the "is this an enemy" test says a player is never an enemy of a Troll_Summoned (they still fight everything else). This also stops their swings hurting players. Summons already out keep working the same way after the update, no recast needed. Note: 1.51.38 was aimed at the wrong staff (Dead Raiser) and stays, it is harmless.
  1.51.38 FIX (30. Dead Raiser): the Troll (and other mini bosses) summoned by the staff at level 3 and 4 also attacked the player. A summon now joins the players faction when it is made, and a check on the game "is this an enemy" test makes sure a summon and a player are never enemies of each other. Summons made before this version are not changed: dismiss them (middle click) and cast again.
  1.51.37 FIX: shared chest (13. Chests / AllowSharedChestAccess). The second player could open the chest, but it moved the chest ownership to them and the game closed the window of the first player (it only keeps a chest window open for the owner); opening again swapped it back. While the game decides whether to keep the chest window showing, the chest you have open now counts as yours, so both players keep their window. Saving and loading still use the real owner, and a change by the player who is not the owner takes ownership back and saves it. Both players moving items at the very same moment can still clash (see the setting description). If it still kicks, send the log: a line "[SharedChest] Container.IsOwner not found" would mean this game version asks a different way.
  1.51.36 NEW (25. Armor Colors): two cape-only effects, Frostfire (ice blue and flame orange trading places along the cape) and Thunderblood (dark blood red struck by flashes of lightning). Pick the Cape tab, then the effect. They show on the cape smoke and glow like the other effects, and the Dimmer slider dims them (Size and Smoke too); Solid / Pulse still apply. They are not offered for the chest, legs or helmet, and other players with the mod see them on your cape.
  1.51.35 FIX (from your log of v1.51.34): items in the food (quick) slots, the recycle and trash cells, and the gear slots losing their items. The log showed the character is loaded with 4 rows and the game then sets 6; the saved items of rows 5 and 6 were read into the gear/quick/recycle/trash cells, and the real gear items had no room. Now the inventory has room for every row while the saved items are read, so each item comes back where it was saved; when the game sets the rows the gear and quick rows go right under them (the number of rows at save time is stored in the character data, key AgelessGearBase), and anything sitting in a cell that cannot hold it (recycle/trash cells, wrong type) is moved to a free normal cell. Log lines: "[GearSlots] reading the saved items with room for 14 rows" and "[GearSlots] rows set: ...". Items that are already in the wrong cell from the earlier sessions are moved out at your next login.
  1.51.34 FIX: compile error "Operator ! cannot be applied to operand of type void" (Inventory.RemoveItem returns nothing in this game version) in the 1.51.32 take-and-keep helper. The removal is now checked by counting the items before and after.
  1.51.33 FIX (from your log of v1.51.30): the auto feed broke because game 1.0.20 changed the smelter RPC_AddFuel: it now reads an extra true/false value, and the old call without it threw "EndOfStreamException: Unable to read beyond the end of the stream" - AFTER the item had left the chest (so fuel/ore vanished) and it stopped the feed for every other smelter in that pass (so nothing fed). The feed now reads the game real parameter list (logged once: "[SmelterFeed] game RPC_AddFuel(...)") and fills every argument. If a call still fails, the item is put back in the chest and the other smelters carry on. NOTE from the same log: the Frost Kiln (piece_FrostKiln) uses Ice as its FUEL, so it is fed from your fuel chests (mark one holding Ice) and not from ordinary chests.
  1.51.32 FIX: ore (or fuel) taken from a chest by the auto feed could vanish when the smelter did not accept it (the game quietly ignores an add it does not want). The feed now checks that the smelter really took the item (its queue or fuel went up) and, if not, puts the item straight back in the chest. A line "[SmelterFeed] ... refused ..." (one a minute) names the station and why, which shows what the smelter did not like.
  1.51.31 PERFORMANCE (stutter in a big base): the station-upgrade level check (the part that lets upgrades count at any distance) ran for every crafting station in range on every frame, each time looping over every upgrade piece in the world with reflection. The level is now worked out at most once a second per station, and the list of upgrade pieces is refreshed every 5 s instead of 2 s. If the stutter (a 2 s drop every few minutes) remains, send the log: lines starting [Perf] name the mod job that was slow.
  1.51.30 CHEST SEARCH / CHESTS: (1) The flash no longer lights up the area: the point light is gone. The chest itself glows (pulsing emission in the flash colour) and a thin beam marks it. (2) The on-screen marker now starts with the chest name, e.g. "Fuel chest: Iron ingot x40   12 m" (the name you gave the chest, or the default), for the automatic flash and the per-chest Flash button. (3) HARDENING for items vanishing from chests after the area unloads and reloads: every change the mod makes to a chest (auto feed, deposits, loot, search Take, chest-to-chest moves) is now written to the chest saved data straight away, and the mod no longer changes a chest it could not take ownership of (the game does not save such a change). If items still vanish, tell me what was happening (auto feed on? a kiln near the chest? another player nearby?) and send the log.
  1.51.29 AUTO FEED: Frigid Kiln check. The Frigid Kiln (Ice -> Liquid Frost, no fuel) is a smelter-type station, so it is fed Ice from nearby chests by the normal smelter feed (any chest in range, no fuel chest needed). The log now lists each kind of station once, e.g. "[SmelterFeed] auto-feeding 'piece_frigidkiln' (fuel: none, takes: $item_ice)", so you can see it was picked up. If it is NOT listed, it is not a Smelter in this game version: send the log.
  1.51.28 FIX: smelter/kiln auto feed did nothing when the smelter was owned by another peer or an earlier session (it silently skipped it). It now takes ownership first, as the shield generator feed does, and feeds from the next tick. New log lines "[SmelterFeed] ..." (one a minute) say why nothing is fed (no valid view, no usable chest in range).
  1.51.27 FIX (second try): chest names still showed through the hammer build menu, because the game build menu field was not found under the name I guessed. Names (and chest-search markers) are now hidden whenever the mouse cursor is visible, which is the case with any game window open (build menu, inventory, map, menu); the build menu window is also looked up by a name containing "pieceselection" as a second check.
  1.51.26 FIX: chest names (and the chest-search markers) showed through the hammer build menu. They are now hidden while the build menu is open, and still show through walls in the normal view.
  1.51.25 FIX (chest search): the search panel covered the item tooltip. The panel is drawn above the game windows, so it now steps aside while a tooltip is showing, unless the mouse is on the panel itself.
  1.51.24 NEW (chest search): (1) Recent searches: the last 6 searches that found something are shown as buttons under the search box while it is empty (one click searches again), kept in the cfg (33. Chest Search / RecentSearches) so they survive a restart, with a Clear button. (2) Where it came from: after you take items, the message says which chests they came from (name and distance), and those chests glow green for 8 seconds with a label such as "Took 40 Iron". (3) FIX inside the panel: button clicks no longer change the window in the middle of the same frame (avoids IMGUI layout errors); they now run at the start of the next frame.
  1.51.23 NEW: chest search. A search bar to the right of the chest window (below the Fuel and Name buttons). Type an item name: after a short pause the chests nearby that hold it flash for 30 seconds, or until you open them: a pulsing light, a tall beam of light, and an on-screen label with the item, the amount and the distance that shows through walls (an arrow points to chests that are off screen). The flash carries on after you close the window, so you can walk to the chest. Several words must all match; if nothing matches every word the items matching some of them are shown, and a plural s is ignored. The list shows each item with its total and the chests that hold it, nearest first, with a Flash button and a Take button per chest, and an Amount box (with 1, 10, Stack and All) and a button to take from the nearest chests until the amount is reached or your inventory is full. Wards and private chests are respected. Ctrl+F jumps to the search box; while you type, the game keys are held back. New cfg section 33. Chest Search (EnableChestSearch, SearchRange 50, FlashSeconds 30, MaxFlashingChests 10, PanelWidth, PanelOffsetX, PanelOffsetY, FocusKey).
  1.51.22 FIX: compile error in 1.51.21 ("The name Localization does not exist"). The Red hammer message now uses the mod own name-lookup helper instead of naming the game class directly.
  1.51.21 CHANGE: Red hammer rework. Middle click (the remove click) now removes only the piece you are looking at and drops its building materials (a chest that still holds items, or anything inside a ward you cannot use, is left alone). Hold Shift while you middle click to tear down the whole building, as before. Breakable parts that are not build pieces (wood frames, ruin parts, destructibles) are now broken the way the game breaks them, so they drop their normal loot; rock formations still go without loot in a whole-building demolish. Cfg 28. Building Demolish description updated.
  1.51.20 PERFORMANCE (no change in behaviour): the gear-slot layout used to redo every cell label, border and position on every frame while the inventory was open; it now only changes what actually changed (labels cached per cell, positions only written when they moved, borders checked once, the cell list field looked up once). The HUD quick slots only write their size and position when they change. The hotkey input check is worked out once per frame instead of many times. The slow-job timer in the log no longer creates an object on every call.
  1.51.19 FIX: a chest stacked on another chest broke at once. The game builds chests so they pass no support to what rests on them, so the structure check destroyed the top chest. Chests now pass support on (log: "[ChestStack] chests now pass support on ..."). Works for chests that were already placed too.
  1.51.18 NEW: chest stacking. With a chest selected in the hammer, aim at the top of another chest and the new chest sits flush on it, centred and turned the same way, and is marked valid even though the two touch. Cfg 32. Chest Stacking / EnableChestStacking (true). Log note if it fails: "[ChestStack] ...".
  1.51.17 CLEANUP: no change in behaviour. Removed code that was no longer used (the set-aside step of 1.51.15, an unused particle helper, the always-false recycle/trash branch in the gear layout). The version history moved out of the .cs header into this file. Optional split: the plugin as one file per feature (folder AgelessOne_src); use either the single FirstModPlugin.cs or the folder, never both.
  1.51.16 FIX (from the log of v1.51.15): the login drop still happened. The log shows the game Humanoid.DropInvalidItems (called from inside Player.SetInventorySize) takes off and drops the WORN pieces even after they were taken out of the item list, so it judges the equipped items themselves, not the inventory list. Making the inventory taller (1.51.14) and setting the items aside (1.51.15) both failed. Now the check is skipped for the local player (log: "[GearSlots] skipped the game drop-invalid-items check ...") and the extra rows are added again right after SetInventorySize returns. The set-aside step of 1.51.15 is no longer used.
  1.51.15 FIX (from the log of v1.51.14): the login drop still happened. The log showed the game calls DropInvalidItems from INSIDE Player.SetInventorySize, and that making the inventory taller first did not stop it. Now the items of the gear and quick rows are taken out of the item list for the duration of SetInventorySize and put back as soon as it returns, at the right place for whatever number of rows the game set (log: "[GearSlots] set aside N item(s)..." and "put N item(s) back ..."). Nothing is in those rows while the game checks, so nothing is dropped. The DropInvalidItems hook of 1.51.14 was removed, because it made the next step read the mod own extension as the size the game had set.
  1.51.14 FIX (the real cause of armor and quick slots being dropped at login, found from other inventory mods' bug reports for game 1.0.12+): on every spawn the game calls Player.SetInventorySize (back to the normal rows) and then Humanoid.DropInvalidItems, which drops every item sitting below the last row onto the ground. The extra rows are now added again right after SetInventorySize and again right before DropInvalidItems, and if the game changes the number of normal rows (rows bought from the trader) the gear rows move with it. Items already dropped by earlier versions are on the ground where you logged in: pick them up.
  1.51.13 FIX: armor still taken off at login. (1) The layout (what sits in each gear and quick slot) is now stored in the character own saved data (key AgelessGearLayout). After a login, anything that the game moved out of its slot is found again by name and quality and put back (log: "[GearSlots] put ... back into gear slot N"), and the normal wearing code puts it on. (2) The Inventory.Load hook no longer depends only on the inventory being called "Inventory": while the character is loading it extends the inventory it is given. (3) For the first 12 armor take-offs the log names the code that did it ("[GearSlots] ... was taken off by: ...").
  1.51.12 CHANGE: armor glow removed by default. New cfg 25. Armor Colors / GlowEnabled (false): helmet, chest and legs no longer glow (no glowing cloth, no outer halo, no light); an armor effect now shows only as the smoke off the cape. Set GlowEnabled=true to bring the old glow back on those pieces.
  1.51.11 FIX: armor taken off every time a character is loaded. The extra gear rows are now added to the player inventory by a hook on Inventory.Load itself (before the saved items are read in), so the loading path used by game 1.0.20 cannot move gear items out of their slots. As a safety net, worn gear that ends up in the normal grid is moved back into its empty gear slot (log: "[GearSlots] moved worn ... back into its gear slot").
  1.51.10 FIX: a huge white glow on the player that no slider changed. The outer glow picks an "additive" shader; in 1.0.20 the usual ones are not available, and the fallback search could pick a shader whose colour cannot be set, so it drew at full white brightness. A shader is now only used if it accepts _TintColor or _Color; otherwise the glow uses the plain alpha-blended fallback, which the Dimmer slider controls.
  1.51.9  FIX: log warning "AccessTools.Method: Could not find method for type Inventory and name Changed". The game inventory Changed() method is gone in 1.0.20, so moves done by the mod (right-click equip, trash, recycle, sort) did not refresh the window. They now go through InvUtil.Changed, which finds the replacement (a method with Changed in its name, or the change event) and logs which one it used ("[Inventory] change notification: ...").
  1.51.8  FIX (from the log): in game 1.0.20 the inventory cell class is "InventoryElement" with no m_pos/m_go fields. The position is found (Position property), but the "object" guess picked the cell m_selected highlight child instead of the cell itself, so the wrong object was moved. The cell is now the InventoryElement component own game object.
  1.51.7  REBUILT (gear slot setup and layout for game 1.0.20 "Deep North"): (1) the normal inventory height is now remembered per inventory object instead of once for the whole session, and re-learned if the game resets the size, so the gear row can no longer be left "inactive" (which also stopped the gear being worn and the quick slots working); (2) the grid cells are found by the game's cell list, or if that cannot be read, from the grid's child objects; (3) the layout is also applied from the plugin a few times a second while the inventory is open, not only from the game's UpdateGui; (4) if the layout is still not active, an orange box on screen says why.
  1.51.6  DIAGNOSTIC: if the gear layout cannot be applied, the mod now says why in the chat window (3 seconds after opening the inventory) and in the log: the reason, the inventory size, the expected size, and whether the game inventory-grid hook ran at all. Take a screenshot of the chat line.
  1.51.5  FIX: gear slots, quick (food) slots and the recycle/trash cells sat in their raw grid positions with no labels after the 1.0 update. The layout code read the inventory cells through fixed field names (m_elements / m_pos / m_go) and failed silently. It now finds the cell list, each cell position and its object by shape, falls back to list order for the position, and the log says what it found ("[GearSlots] inventory cell type ...", "[GearSlots] layout applied ...") or why it could not apply.
  1.51.4  FIX: "MissingMethodException: Method not found: void Character.Message(MessageHud/MessageType,string,int,Sprite)" (broke Dead Raiser, Auto Sort and the gear-slot drop handling after the game update). On-screen messages now go through Msg.Show, which finds the game's Message method at run time.
  1.51.3  CHECK: reviewed against Valheim patch 1.0.20 (15 Oct 2026: trophy drop chance by star level, cheated-flag cleanup, sheathed weapon attachment points, dedicated-server frame rate, Xbox settings fix). No modding/API changes were listed and the mod touches none of the changed systems, so no code changes were needed; version bumped only.
  1.51.2  FIX: "MissingMethodException: Method not found: int StringExtensionMethods.GetStableHashCode(string,bool)" from RedHammerAwakePatch / RedHammerCopyDbPatch when the game loaded (the Red hammer and the shield-generator fuel were affected). The game's hash method changed its parameters between versions; the mod now uses its own identical copy (StableHash.Of).
  1.51.1  FIX: log error "PATCH FAILED: ArmorColorsBlockRightClickPatch": this game version has no InventoryGrid.OnRightClick, and the palette's right-click blocking is done by the InventoryGui.OnRightClickItem patch, so the failing duplicate was removed.
  1.51.0  NEW: Dundr's damage and reload speed grow with the skill it uses (Elemental Magic). At level 100: damage x2 and reload twice as fast by default (cfg 31. Dundr: SkillScaling, DamageBonusAtLevel100, ReloadSpeedBonusAtLevel100). Log: "[Dundr] skill ... damage x.., reload x.. faster". Note: the game already scales staff damage with skill a little; this is on top.
  1.50.4  FIX: ovens (stone oven) and the auto deposit. Finished food is now also recognised by the game's own "done" status for a slot, and the output-to-chest search also looks at the station's own drop point (an oven drops food further from its centre than a grill). The log now names each cooking station it handles ("[Cooking] output to chest watches 'piece_oven' ...", "[Cooking] took finished food off 'piece_oven' automatically.").
  1.50.3  FIX: Dundr could still not be used by a player without eitr. Its RELOAD also costs eitr (and the shot and draw); every eitr cost of its attacks is now 0, and with Dundr in hand the game's "do you have eitr" check always passes and nothing is taken. No robes needed.
  1.50.2  FIX: Dundr still did not reload while running. Cause (as another mod's notes describe it): while you run, the game clears the player's action queue every tick, and the reload is a queued action. With Dundr in hand a queued reload is now left alone. The log says "[Dundr] kept the reload going instead of cancelling it (running)." the first time it does.
  1.50.1  CHANGE: Dundr reloads at the same speed whether you run or not (cfg 31. Dundr / ReloadWhileRunning). While the game works out Dundr's reload you count as not running. If the log says "[Dundr] did not find the game's weapon reload step", tell me, the game version differs.
  1.50.0  NEW: Dundr (the lightning staff, StaffLightning) costs no eitr, so any player can use it. cfg 31. Dundr: FreeDundr, DundrPrefabNames. The log says "[Dundr] ... no longer costs eitr." when it is applied.
  1.49.1  FIX: the 500 arrow/bolt cap did not apply (stacks still showed 100). The stack size is now raised as soon as the game builds its item list, on a job of its own (it used to share one with other setup jobs), and directly on the arrows and bolts you carry. Look for "[Quiver] ..." lines in the log.
  1.49.0  NEW: a 7th gear slot, the QUIVER (7. Gear Slots / EnableQuiver, QuiverStackSize 500). It takes arrows or bolts, one kind at a time, up to 500, and is worn like the other gear slots so your bow shoots from it. It sits as the third gear row (under the 3+3 slots). To make room, the RECYCLE, TRASH and quick slots moved one row down, and RECYCLE and TRASH now live in the quick-slot row instead of the gear row. All arrows and bolts stack to 500 (also in the normal grid).
  1.48.1  FIX: the cape vapour was too slow and too thin even with the sliders at the top. It now pours down about twice as fast, the clouds are bigger and fuller (a solid centre, soft edge), there are more of them, and Dimmer at the top is now fully thick instead of about a third. Sliders: Size up to 1.5 m clouds, Smoke up to 64 clouds a second, Dimmer = opacity.
  1.48.0  CHANGE: the cape smoke now looks like the vapour that pours off something super cold (liquid nitrogen): a few big soft clouds that leave the back of the cape, swell as they fall, pour down to the ground and roll out along it before fading, instead of many small drops that looked like rain. Size = how big the clouds are, Smoke = how many, Dimmer = how thick / see-through (it no longer changes the count).
  1.47.0  NEW: Smoke slider in the colour palette = how much smoke comes off the cape (number of puffs; cfg 25. Armor Colors / SmokeAmount). Other players with the mod see your setting too.
  1.46.3  FIX: no smoke showed. The smoke now uses its own soft round puff picture and the glow's additive shader instead of the sword's material, and is started explicitly. A line "[ArmorFx] smoke check: playing=..., particles=..., visible=..." is logged 4 s after it starts, so if it still does not show, that line says why.
  1.46.2  FIX: the cape smoke came off in a ring around you, and the Size slider did nothing for it. The smoke is now its own small emitter, a thin box on the back of the player where the cape hangs, so it can only start there. Size, Dimmer and the colour all drive it directly.
  1.46.1  FIX: the cape smoke spread out like a bubble. It is now small puffs that come straight off the cloth (no outward push, no spread, a capped puff size, almost no sideways drift) and fall about 1 m to your feet; far more of them, much smaller and fainter, so the cape looks like it is turning to smoke. SmokeGroundSeconds default is now 1 s (a saved config keeps its own value).
  1.46.0  CHANGE: the cape effect is now smoke only: a soft smoke in the chosen colour flows down off the cape (never up), lands on the ground, lies there SmokeGroundSeconds (2 s) and fades smoothly. No glow on the cloth itself (CapeSmokeOnly=false brings it back). The Dimmer slider sets how many / how big / how faint the puffs are; Size makes them larger. Other armor pieces keep their glow.
  1.45.2  NEW: Dead Raiser summons keep their distance while following you (cfg 30. Dead Raiser / FollowDistance, default 8 m; the game lets them come within about 3 m). Spawn distance is SummonDistance.
  1.45.1  FIX: shield generators were not fed from fuel chests. The feed now reads the fuel and its maximum straight from the generator (the maximum is a whole number in the game, which broke the old reading), adds the fuel itself instead of calling a game message that may not match, and takes ownership of the generator first. The log now says why it does not feed ("[ShieldFeed] ...": no marked chest in range, chest holds no fuel, ...).
  1.45.0  NEW: a fuelled shield generator's bubble destroys hostile creatures (ones with attack AI that are enemies of the player) that touch it. Not players, tamed creatures, animals or (by default) bosses. cfg 5. Automation: ShieldGeneratorKillsEnemies, ShieldKillsBosses.
  1.44.0  NEW: shield generators are fed fuel from marked FUEL chests only (5. Automation / EnableShieldGeneratorFeed). Dead Raiser: summons appear SummonDistance (8 m) away from you instead of on top of you, last 5 minutes by default, and a middle click with the staff in hand dismisses them.
  1.43.3  Red hammer: now works on Ashlands (and other world) structures. Besides build pieces and WearNTear parts it takes down breakable destructibles and rock formations (MineRock / MineRock5) within SweepRadius, and parts with no network data are removed on your machine instead of being skipped. For a big fortress, raise 28. Building Demolish / SweepRadius.
  1.43.2  FIX: Dead Raiser summons did not change. The staff does not use a flying projectile; it spawns the friendly skeleton next to you. The mod now notices that skeleton appearing (while you hold the staff at level 2+) and swaps it for the level's summons. The log says '[DeadRaiser] level N cast ...' once it has worked.
  1.43.1  FIX: the glow Size slider showed no change. A wider halo is now given more strength (it was spread too thin to see), pieces whose mesh mods can't read get a scaled copy so they resize too, and the log names any piece that can't change size ('[ArmorFx] the mesh ... can't be read').
  1.43.0  NEW: Dead Raiser levels. Level 1 = the normal skeleton; 2 = four random land creatures of your biome; 3 = up to three mini bosses; 4 = like 3 but stronger (extra stars). Never water creatures. Summons are tamed, follow you, drop no loot, and fade after SummonSeconds (max MaxActiveSummons at once). cfg: 30. Dead Raiser.
  1.42.0  NEW: a Size slider (under Dimmer in the Colours window; cfg 25. Armor Colors / EffectRadius, 0.2-3, default 1) sets how far the glow reaches out from the armor. It resizes the edge halo, the cape particles and the optional light. Others with the mod see your size.
  1.41.0  SUBTLE GLOW: the big pool of light on the ground was the small lights beside each piece; they are now OFF by default (cfg 25. Armor Colors / AuraLight) so the glow stays on the body. The edge halo is tighter and fainter, the emission is lower, the particles are small drifting motes, and the baked glow on chest/legs is milder. New default Dimmer 0.4 (a value you saved earlier in the cfg overrides it: lower EffectBrightness or use the slider).
  1.40.0  The cape particles now borrow the Mistwalker sword's mist effect instead of Frostner's frost (Frostner is only a fallback if Mistwalker's effect can't be found). The log says which one was used.
  1.39.3  The Colours palette now closes when you close the inventory (Tab), if it was opened from the inventory.
  1.39.2  The Dimmer slider now also controls the cape particles: lower = more see-through, smaller and fewer particles (the particle glow was far too strong). The default dimmer level shows far less than before.
  1.39.1  PERF FIX (the many '[Perf] ... took N ms' warnings): the real cause is removed instead of hidden. Sails and BirdRemoval searched the whole scene every few seconds (about 20 ms each); boats and birds are now noted when they are created, and a boat's sails are looked up once. SmelterAutoFeed, OutputDeposit and the other station jobs asked the physics engine for every collider within 40 m; stations and chests are now kept in a list as they are created. Same behaviour, a fraction of the time.
  1.39.0  NEW: Eitr armor. Wearing eitr armor (mage robes: anything with an eitr bonus, or a Mage item) gives eitr without eating: 200 to start, +100 for every upgrade level of the best eitr piece worn; spells do not use up the bar while it is worn; the bar starts full when you put it on. NEW: frost-like particles (borrowed from Frostner) drift off the cape in the glow colour, cape only. cfg: 29. Eitr Armor, and 25. Armor Colors / CapeParticles.
  1.38.1  FIX: the outer glow had a hard edge. It is now five stacked layers, each bigger and dimmer than the last, so the halo fades out softly (feathered). Make it softer/tighter by changing the brightness (Dimmer) slider.
  1.38.0  Armor glow now has a real OUTER glow (like Bone Snap): each glowing cape/helmet piece gets a slightly bigger additive copy around it, so a bright halo shows outside its outline. Chest and legs (drawn on the body) keep the baked glow plus the lights. The log says which shader the halo uses ('[ArmorFx] glow shell uses shader ...').
  1.37.0  Armor glow per piece: the glow effect can be set on each piece on its own (chest, legs, helmet, cape; the Colours window's tabs choose which, "All" sets every piece). And it now looks like a glow: HDR emission that keeps the piece's pattern (bloom makes the halo), a coloured light beside each piece, and chest/legs get a bright glow baked into their texture. Pulse animates the cape/helmet/lights; chest and legs stay steady. cfg Effect is now chest|legs|helmet|cape.
  1.36.1  FIX: clicks on the Colours palette also went through to the inventory underneath (picking up items). Inventory clicks are now ignored while the mouse is over the palette window.
  1.36.0  Armor glow reworked: it is now a bright glow all over the worn armor (like a magic weapon's glow) instead of a small light. Effects: Colour (your armor colour), Poison, Fire, Blood, NEW Frost. Choose Solid or Pulse, and a Dimmer slider sets the brightness. Saved as 25. Armor Colors / Effect, EffectStyle, EffectBrightness. Others with the mod see it. The log says once which shader/emission the armor uses ('[ArmorFx] shader ...').
  1.35.0  Armor colours: (1) the Feather cloak (cape) colour is much brighter and clearer: its dark texture is lifted before tinting. (2) NEW visual effects row in the Colours palette: Pulse, Poison, Fire, Blood (an animated glow on your armor; looks only, no stats). Other players with the mod see it. cfg: 25. Armor Colors / Effect.
  1.34.0  NEW: sap extractors empty themselves when full, and the sap goes into the nearest chest (same rules as smelter output: a chest already holding sap first, else the nearest with room). Only while a chest can take it. cfg: 11. Station Output & Upgrades / EnableSapCollectorOutput.
  1.33.0  Armor colours: the Cape tab now recolours cloaks properly, including the Feather cloak. Besides the colour it now tints the cloak's picture (a tinted copy, the original is untouched), since the Feather cloak's look comes mostly from its texture.
  1.32.7  FIX: the Red hammer was aiming at your own character (the camera ray starts behind you). It now ignores your body, prefers the piece the game is highlighting, and only plays the swing when a demolish actually started.
  1.32.6  Red hammer: when you hit something that is not a build piece, the log now says exactly what it is ('[Demolish] Hit non-piece object ...'), and breakable non-piece objects are removed.
  1.32.5  Red hammer: the wood frame was left standing. Now everything breakable within SweepRadius (default 20 m) of the spot you hit is taken down too, touching or not, including loose wooden frame parts that are not normal build pieces. New cfg: 28. Building Demolish / SweepRadius.
  1.32.4  Red hammer: if you hit scenery (a world ruin pillar, not a build piece) it now starts from the nearest build piece within 8 m, otherwise says it is scenery.
  1.32.3  FIX: the Red hammer demolish left parts of buildings (wood beams/pillars) standing. It now links pieces from the game's list of all loaded pieces by touching or near-touching bounds, and logs why any piece stayed ([Demolish] Removed ...). LinkGap default is now 2.
  1.32.2  FIX: the Red hammer's icon was blank. The red picture is now made more carefully (and checked); if it comes out empty the normal hammer picture is used instead.
  1.32.1  FIX: the crafted Red hammer did not appear in the inventory and had no icon. The item is now made findable by name in every lookup table of the item database,
          its picture is kept from being cleaned up, and the log says whether the game can find it ('[RedHammer] Registered ...').
  1.32.0  CHANGE: the whole-building demolish moved from Ctrl + middle click on the normal hammer to a new craftable RED HAMMER (workbench; RedHammerCost, RedHammerStationLevel).
          It builds like the normal hammer; its remove click demolishes the whole building you aim at, no hotkey. The normal hammer is back to normal.
  1.31.2  FIX: the building demolish did nothing: the hammer was not recognised (it is a tool, so the game's 'current weapon' is not the hammer). It now looks at what is equipped,
          and says 'Take out the build hammer first' when Ctrl + middle click is used without it.
  1.31.1  FIX: compile error (the hammer is now found through GetCurrentWeapon).
  1.31.0  NEW: demolish a whole building. Hold the build hammer, hold Ctrl and click the middle mouse button on a building (yours, or a Dverger outpost, a Seeker
          hideout, ...): every connected piece is found and removed a few at a time (no lag), each dropping its building materials as loot. Chests with items inside and
          pieces in a ward you can't use are left standing. New section 28 (EnableBuildingDemolish, DemolishRange, MaxPieces, MaxRadius, LinkGap, PiecesPerStep, StepSeconds, RespectWards).
  1.30.1  FIX: the farming grid on the ground no longer bounces up and down. Its height now comes from the terrain itself instead of from the exact spot you aim at, so it stays put when you move to another square.
  1.30.0  NEW: other players now see your armor colours (and you see theirs). Your colours are published on your player; every player needs this mod to see them.
  1.29.1  FIX: the armor colour palette window is now solid (it was see-through).
  1.29.0  CHANGE: (1) an enchantment now also costs coins (CoinCost, default 100, scaled with the weapon like the materials) and the full cost is written in the
          Enchant tab. (2) A weapon can only be enchanted ONCE: an enchanted weapon can't be changed or replaced. (3) The Sort and Colours buttons are now copies of the
          game's tab buttons, so they look like the Craft / Upgrade / Enchant tabs.
  1.28.4  FIX: a flash of the plain panel just before the Enchant tab appeared. The tab is now built at the click, and the plain panel is only used if building it fails.
  1.28.3  FIX: the Enchant tab started too far right, so its buttons sat on top of the weapon list and the game's own list was still showing. It now starts where
          the game's recipe rows start.
  1.28.2  FIX: the Enchant tab was not visible at all once opened (its top layer was set below the game's window). It now takes the game's sorting layer and goes above it.
  1.28.1  FIX: the Enchant tab was drawn under the game's own list and details, and was too wide. It now sits on its own top layer and is sized from the
          game's recipe list and craft button.
  1.28.0  CHANGE: the Enchant tab is now built from copies of the game's own crafting window pieces (recipe rows, title, description, ingredient
          slots, tab buttons and the big craft button), so it looks like the Upgrade tab. The plain panel stays as a fallback if the game's pieces are not found.
  1.27.3  CHANGE: the Enchant window now uses the game's own look (its crafting panel background, tab button picture and font) instead of the plain grey box.
  1.27.2  CHANGE: the Enchant tab is now a copy of the game's own tab, so it looks and behaves like the Craft and Upgrade tabs (the open tab is greyed out like theirs).
  1.27.1  FIX: compile error (item names are translated without needing the Localization class directly).
  1.27.0  CHANGE: weapon enchants moved to an Enchant tab at the forge (replaces the panel from 1.25.0 in the recipe list). Pick any weapon you
          carry and an effect, pay the cost (which grows with the weapon's damage, CostScalesWithWeapon), and it is enchanted. Replacing an effect is allowed.
  1.26.0  CHANGE: the armor colour palette opens from a Colours button next to the Sort button in the inventory window. The F7 hotkey is now
          optional (PaletteHotkey is empty by default); new setting ColorsButtonOffsetX.
  1.25.2  FIX: the weapon effect panel was not showing in the crafting window. The selected recipe is now found by type (not only by name), the panel is drawn with fixed positions on top of everything, and it logs when it appears.
  1.25.1  FIX: compile errors (particle renderer type, Escape key check).
  1.25.0  NEW: weapon enchants. When you craft a weapon you can pick a fire, frost, lightning, poison, spirit or life steal effect
