          ChainRecipeCost, ChainRecipeAmount, ChainRecipeStationLevel.
  1.20.0  NEW: the farming grid is now drawn on the ground while you plant: a square around every spot a plant will go, hugging
          the terrain and fading out with distance, with the spot you are aiming at in the middle. New settings in section 19:
          ShowFarmGrid, FarmGridShowRadius, FarmGridLineColor, FarmGridLineWidth.
  1.19.1  FIX: the farming grid made the plant preview (the ghost) vanish. The snapped spot started at height 0 and kept it whenever
          the ground lookup failed, which buries the preview underground; it also sank it on floors and raised beds. The
          height now stays where you aimed and only follows the change in ground height between that spot and the snapped one.
  1.19.0  NEW: chest names. A "Name chest" button in the chest window lets you type a name for any chest; the name is shown as
          floating text over the chest (like an ESP) for every chest within ChestLabelDistance, optionally through walls, and
          also in the chest's hover text. New section 23: EnableChestNames, ChestLabelDistance, ChestLabelThroughWalls,
          ChestLabelFontSize, ChestLabelColor, ChestLabelShowDistance, ChestLabelHeight, ChestNameMaxLength, ChestNameButtonY.
  1.18.0  NEW: birds can be removed (RemoveBirds: crows, seagulls and the like no longer spawn, and ones already in the world are
          deleted) and replaced by a buildable FEATHER COLLECTOR (hammer, Furniture tab). It is a small container that slowly fills
          with Feathers while a tree is nearby. New section 22: RemoveBirds, EnableFeatherCollector, FeatherCollectorCost,
          FeatherIntervalMinutes, FeathersPerCycle, FeatherRequireTree, FeatherTreeRange, FeatherMaxCatchUpCycles.
          Collectors are never used as a target by auto sort or station output.
  1.17.0  CHANGE: smelter, kiln and furnace output (and cooked food) now goes to the chest that already holds that item, looked
          for out to OutputHomeChestRange (default 40 m) from the station, not just the nearest chest. Only if no chest holds
          it does the old "nearest chest with room" fallback apply (OutputChestRange, OutputFallbackAnyChest). Fuel chests never
          receive output. The chest that receives items plays the auto sort sound/glow. New setting: OutputHomeChestRange.
  1.16.1  PERFORMANCE (stutter): the once-a-second spike is gone. The background jobs now take turns, one per short step,
          instead of all running in the same frame. Area scans no longer allocate memory or look every collider up again
          every time. Window/HUD parts (auto sort, chest button, sort button, quick slot HUD) update 10x a second instead of
          every frame. Sails and station upgrades are looked up every 2 s. Station output no longer builds new lists on every
          tick. The inventory layout reads its cell fields without reflection every frame. NEW: slow-feature log
          (LogSlowFeatures / SlowFeatureMs) writes "[Perf] <feature> took X ms" so any remaining hitch can be traced.
  1.16.0  CHANGE: the loot vacuum stops pulling items in once you are carrying your maximum weight, and skips any item that
          would push you over it. New setting: LootVacuumStopAtMaxWeight.
  1.15.1  DEFAULTS: new default values taken from the owner's own config: AutoSortRange 30, InstantSort off, GlowIntensity 5,
          ShowMessage (auto sort) on, Gamma 0.6, GammaUseVeil off, FuelChestStrict on, SkillXpMultiplier 5, GridSize 0.5,
          FarmGridSpacing 1.25, CraftingChestPullRange 30, VeinMineKey LeftShift, LootVacuumRange 7.
  1.15.0  CHANGE: the farming grid now sizes itself automatically. Spacing = the largest grow radius among the plant you
          hold and the plants already growing nearby, plus their collider width, so every plant keeps room to grow even
          when you mix crops. The grid lines up with the nearest existing plant, and a spot where the game would still
          refuse to grow is shifted to the nearest cell that works. New setting: FarmGridAuto.
  1.14.0  NEW: quick slots are also shown on the HUD next to the boss power (bottom left), with item icon, stack
